# The lockfile is written by pnpm, not by a human, and pnpm's format is not
# Prettier's. Left to itself `pnpm format` rewrites all seven thousand lines of
# it — single quotes to double, blank lines stripped — and the next `pnpm
# install` writes them all back. That is a permanent diff nobody can win, sitting
# on top of the one file where a spurious change is hardest to review.
#
# This said `package-lock.json` until now, from before the project moved to pnpm,
# which is exactly why nothing caught it.
pnpm-lock.yaml
